  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `README.md`: a new subsection `### How you can help, by AI budget` in \"Contributing\", after \"Tools\". It has four parts:\n  1. A table of budget tiers. Each row gives the work to pick and the work to avoid.\n  2. \"If you run out of quota\": open a draft PR, tick \"Allow edits by maintainers\", comment `help me finish`.\n  3. \"You do not need a big disk\": the review machines build and test each PR.\n  4. The fork flow in four steps. It also says: do not push to `NeoTech/Camcraft`, and ask ownership questions on the PR.\n- The Contributing intro links to the new subsection one time.\n- `docs/decisions/4403-readme-ai-budget.md`: the decision record.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe README did not tell a contributor which work fits an AI plan. It did not say what to do when the quota ends.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Docs only. There is no pinning test, and no mutation check applies.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: the plan has 0 steps (\"nothing in crates/ changed\").\n- The README still contains the donation URL. The test `donate_link_matches_the_published_project_funding_link` reads the README for that URL.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff changes no code, no post and no toolpath, so no golden or catalog suite can change. I did not run the catalog suites.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The rendered Markdown on GitHub (the table and the anchor link). The anchor follows the GitHub heading slug rules.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches no crate.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `README.md`.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #4403\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
